<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Longanus River</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">260s BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Longanus River was fought in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the 260s BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiero-ii-of-syracuse">Hieron II of Syracuse</a> and the Mamertines, Campanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> who held Messana. Hieron's victory broke Mamertine power and led him to take the title of king. The Mamertines then appealed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> for help, an appeal that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a>.</p></div>
